.doctype {paged}
.include {metadata.qd}
.include {../loader.qd}

.formatpagenumber {i}

.lmecover \
    title:{Example Thesis Title for the FAU-LME Quarkdown Theme} \
    author:{Sample Author} \
    birthdate:{1. Januar 2000} \
    birthplace:{Example City} \
    advisor:{Advisor Name} \
    started:{1. Januar 2026} \
    finished:{30. Juni 2026} \
    doctype:{mt}

.pagemargin {topoutsidecorner}
    .currentpage

#! Abstract

This is a one-paragraph example abstract that demonstrates the small centered
bold heading style used for unnumbered front-matter sections.

.formatpagenumber {1}
.resetpagenumber {1}

.pagemargin {topoutside}
    *.lastheading depth:{1}*

# Introduction

This chapter exercises the two-line chapter-opening layout: "Chapter N" prefix
above the bold title with the LaTeX-equivalent vertical drop.

## Math macros

Inline math: $ \mat{A} \transp{\vec{x}} = \vec{b} $ where $ \vec{x} \in \real^n $.

Display math:

$$$
\argmax_{\theta \in \integers} \mathcal{L}(\theta) = \sum_{i=1}^{n} \norm{\hat{x}_i - x_i}
$$$

## A bullet list

- First item with the discreet small-bullet marker.
- Second item.
- Third item.

## A booktabs-style table

| Method | Result | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Baseline | 0.72 | reference |
| Proposed | 0.91 | this work |

## A citation

Per Peffers .cite {peffers2007dsr} the artifact-centric approach is appropriate.

## A long fenced code block (regression: page-spanning `<pre>`)

The block below exists to verify that long fenced code blocks paginate
across page boundaries instead of being clipped or dropped (theme v0.2.1
fix in `styles.css` overrides Quarkdown's screen-mode
`pre code { overflow: hidden }`). A theme consumer rebuilding this
example should see all rows from `row_1` through `row_60` in the
produced PDF; if any row is missing, the override regressed.

```json
{
  "long_listing_regression": {
    "purpose": "verify that pre/code blocks longer than a page split correctly",
    "rows": [
      {"id": "row_1",  "value": 1,  "label": "alpha"},
